# Build-context hygiene for docker/gotth.Dockerfile, whose context is the
# GOTTH-LIVE ROOT (the apps' go.mod `replace` onto the checkout is what makes
# them measure the working tree, so the library source has to be in the
# context). bench/.dockerignore is next.Dockerfile's, whose context stops at
# bench/; this file is BuildKit's per-Dockerfile form so the two do not have to
# be one file serving two different context roots.
#
# The fixtures are excluded on purpose: they are ~13 MB of derived JSONL and
# docker/compose.yaml MOUNTS them read-only into the measured container rather
# than baking them in, so both stacks' containers read the same bytes from the
# same path and "both servers read the same bytes" (§2.5) is a property of the
# topology instead of two Dockerfiles agreeing.
#
# .git is excluded because it is large and because nothing in the build reads
# it — which is also why the build passes -buildvcs=false rather than letting Go
# discover it is not in a repository.

.git
.github

# node lives only under bench/ (FR-74) and none of it belongs in a Go build.
**/node_modules
bench/apps/*/next
bench/analyze
bench/audit
bench/data
bench/fixtures/*/ticks.jsonl

# The proxy's local key and certificate. §3.6 puts TLS outside the measured
# container; the one thing worse than a key in an image is a key in an image
# that was excluded from the tree it was committed to.
bench/docker/tls

# Not read by the build: prose, the other modules, and this tree's own tooling.
docs
examples
test/memory
tools
gotth-live
*.log
